{
  "$schema": "../dialogue.schema.json",
  "id": "cray-customs",
  "notes": "mw-e39.20: Inspector Prudence Cray (bible 5.13), Lantern Court customs. Incorruptible: every bribe option sets cray.bribe.attempted, lowers disposition by 6 and is recorded; no branch lets a bribe succeed (AC-2). Never confiscates plot-critical or forbidden-plot items: the confiscate hook is an emit whose payload excludes both (AC-5). Sorcerer is searched on sight; romance novels (stand-in fact cray.romance-brought) raise disposition; evidence about bay nine (stand-in facts evidence.*) opens the legal seizure route; cold disposition still accepts evidence. mw-e39.22 (The Tidefair, Contraband Pages): ask-crate names the impounded crate (books.impounded, also set by the sorcerer search); ask-swap releases the books after the romance novel (cray.books-traded); present-writ checks a writ (Vane's passes, Mirela's forged seal passes unless the player already tried a bribe); ask-regatta explains rule four; entries thanks, regatta-fine, pocket-ribbon and theft-noticed react to the quests' facts. Still incorruptible: no bribe works.",
  "speakers": [
    {
      "id": "cray",
      "npc": "npc-cray"
    }
  ],
  "entries": [
